   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Before it sends or receives data, the 8251A must be loaded with control words that define its function; they must immediately follow a reset, internal or external.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "549-555",
       "sha": "3eb918b4830b94d788182fbe5b28b5f1718d6d6c749d567c1c5390168de3a5e2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The control words come in two formats: the mode instruction and the command instruction.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "556-558",
       "sha": "e39bcedd139db41e825ad9b6a8b64973f54a263b7f09a0cf0fc2bc37d4789d16"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With C/D 1, RD high, WR low and CS low, a write puts the data bus into the control register.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "218",
       "sha": "7723ef19ec239dae942e7ca84ef61274a76e9fc1047cc5ed7a5ee0bc0b1416f6"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "order",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Once the mode instruction has been written, SYNC characters may be written.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "563-565",
       "sha": "42d09a68113c0a2f3a33a010bfe90bd1be459e864270de547a347ecdbb018113"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "order",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The mode instruction must follow a reset, and command instructions may be written after it.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "559-565",
       "sha": "ff41f2d2f9cc24779101cd5e6a23afc33262ac9757941d76be1f936ee21dcc85"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The command instruction defines a word that controls the actual operation of the 8251A.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "566-568",
       "sha": "aa262e86c03689908b03cd71b0caf49a6b75dce619501cd84f31dc87208a394a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "order",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The mode instruction must be written immediately after a reset; every control word written after it loads the command instruction.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "569-575",
       "sha": "bbf7212e4c6c7a5898028f7cddfe535e66f5d6125def1fd21055ed90497b64da"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "order",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The master reset bit of a command instruction starts an internal reset that returns the 8251A to the mode instruction format; commands follow the mode instruction or SYNC characters.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "576-583",
       "sha": "a829d380ee84a43e1e5e19aa492e58211eeb35899225ebf88cc88e02c1251308"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The device can be seen as two components, asynchronous and synchronous, sharing the package; the format can be changed only after a master chip reset.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "584-592",
       "sha": "05b172df5b03147249b2372a8dec5809426010d50d1feb820d128f38ff45ffa4"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "10",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The command instruction controls the actual operation of the selected format, with functions such as enable transmit/receive, error reset and modem controls.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "825-834",
       "sha": "41359bc7d4a6157b09596c55cc6d52948c4b42bcb4cd10492a6dc3f20579461c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "11",
     "on": "order",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "After the mode instruction and any SYNC characters, all further control writes with C/D = 1 load a command instruction; a reset returns the device to the mode instruction format.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "835-840",
       "sha": "f8ad8261407c88cc9483c24b2c9c2852d06a26684423e12f9b9cb9b86a57c99f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "12",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "On power-up the 8251A may start in any format; writing three 00H bytes with C/D = 1 covers the worst case, and an internal reset command (40H) can then follow.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "841-846",
       "sha": "c8aea892a43664c3552b0b06ce88359615060633777cb3827687244d4ff8dddb"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "847-853",
       "sha": "eab41db30456c714c8505897bd358772383062b64c39e3b39c25c129c157c085"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
